# Build context for the worker is the REPO ROOT (RunPod's GitHub integration
# clones the whole repo and builds from its root), but the worker image only
# needs render-worker/. Without this, Docker uploads ~5GB of context — most of
# it public/ models and HDRIs the worker fetches over HTTP at render time, not
# from the image.
#
# Docker picks up "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" in preference to the root
# .dockerignore, so this file applies ONLY to the worker build and leaves the
# app's own .dockerignore (which must keep public/) untouched.

# Exclude everything...
*

# ...then re-include just the worker.
!render-worker/package.json
!render-worker/package-lock.json
!render-worker/check-context.mjs
!render-worker/worker.mjs
!render-worker/runpod-handler.mjs
!render-worker/serve.mjs
!render-worker/entrypoint.sh
